# Legendary: a supertype [CR#205.4a].
#
# [CR#205.4e] "Any instant or sorcery spell with the supertype "legendary" is subject to a casting
# restriction. A player can't cast a legendary instant or sorcery spell unless that player
# controls a legendary creature or a legendary planeswalker." Per holder: while it is an instant
# or sorcery, each player can't cast it unless that player controls one. The rule's "that player"
# cannot be written yet: the `onlyUnless` condition is the conditional's antecedent, which the
# `cant`'s referents do not reach (`docs/decisions/semantics.md` §2.2 item 2). `actorControls`
# stands in for it; whether an "unless" clause reads the Subject of the prohibition it qualifies
# is an open design question.
#
# [CR#205.4d] The legend rule a legendary permanent is subject to is its own row, `legendRule`,
# since card text names it.
supertype legendary {
  lexical = {lemma = "legendary"},
  spelling = "legendary",
  name = "Legendary",
  confers = [
    property(
      asLongAs(
        is(this, isInstantOrSorcery),
        onlyUnless(
          cant(actor(eachPlayer), cast(this)),
          exists(
            and([
                or([
                    and([hasSupertype(legendary), isCreature, isPermanent]),
                    and([hasSupertype(legendary), isPlaneswalker, isPermanent])]),
                actorControls])))))]
}
